  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce from 25% the incidence of TB and from 50% the mortality due to TB by 2019 compared to 2015 - Guinea-Bissau (01-Jul-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guinea-Bissau, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Republic of Guinea-Bissau (MINSAP)This program has the following goals: To reduce TB incidence by 25% and TB mortality by 50% by 2019, compared to 2013. The objectives of this program are: To cure at least 70% of MDR-TB patients on second-line treatment by 2019.  To increase the number of detected TB cases - all forms - from 2,288 in 2014 to 3,437 in 2019.  To increase the proportion of TB / HIV cases treated with ART from 24.8% in 2014 to 90% in 2019.  To increase to at least 90% the treatment success rate among new cases of pulmonary tuberculosis confirmed bacteriologically by 2019.  To strengthen program management and coordination capacity at all levels</narrative>
  </description>
